course: dictionary
lesson: 15991
title: The greatest of all: utmost
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Utmost» means the greatest, or as much as something can possibly be. When something is «of the utmost importance», it matters more than almost anything else. The word tells you how strong the feeling or effort is.
explain: Look at the words near it to check. «Carry the eggs with the utmost care» means you must be as careful as you possibly can. Try swapping in «the most» or «the greatest». If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
explain: «Utmost» can also be a noun, meaning the most you can do. «Ella did her utmost to finish the race.» Her utmost is the best she could possibly manage. Old stories and the Bible use it to mean the farthest, most distant place, as in «the utmost parts of the earth».
fact: «Utmost» means the greatest or most extreme.
fact: «Of the utmost importance» means as important as something can be.
fact: «Do your utmost» means try as hard as you possibly can.
fact: In old stories, «utmost» can mean farthest or most distant, as in «the utmost parts of the earth».
fact: A good check is to swap in «the most» or «the greatest»: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
exercise: «The doctor said the matter was of the utmost importance.» What does utmost mean here? | Very small | Slightly interesting | Not important at all | *The greatest possible
exercise: Mia said, «I will do my utmost to win.» What does her utmost mean? | Her favourite game | Her best friend's name | *The most she can possibly do | The least she can do
exercise: «Take the utmost care when you cross the road.» Find and copy the one word that means greatest. | cross | *utmost | road | take
test: «He showed the utmost kindness to the lost puppy.» What does utmost mean? | Kindness on a Tuesday | No kindness at all | A little bit of kindness | *The greatest kindness possible
test: Old stories say the hero sailed to «the utmost ends of the earth». What does utmost mean here? | *Farthest and most distant | Warmest and sunniest | Most crowded | Nearest and closest
exam: Which sentence uses utmost to mean as much care as possible? | «The bread was left on the table.» | «We walked to the park after lunch.» | *«Carry the eggs with the utmost care.» | «Please keep the room tidy.»
